{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Perfected_Strike","to":"Perfected Strike"},{"from":"Pommel_Strike","to":"Pommel Strike"},{"from":"Ritual_Dagger","to":"Ritual Dagger"},{"from":"Carve_Reality","to":"Carve Reality"},{"from":"Bullet_Time","to":"Bullet Time"},{"from":"Poisoned_Stab","to":"Poisoned Stab"},{"from":"Inner_Peace","to":"Inner Peace"},{"from":"Mental_Fortress","to":"Mental Fortress"},{"from":"Sweeping_Beam","to":"Sweeping Beam"},{"from":"Searing_Blow","to":"Searing Blow"},{"from":"Flame_Barrier","to":"Flame Barrier"}],"pages":{"2025":{"pageid":2025,"ns":0,"title":"Accuracy","revisions":[{"revid":55612,"parentid":55258,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} {{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Accuracy\n|Image       = Green-Accuracy.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} deal (4;6) additional damage.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Accuracy\n|Image        = Icon Accuracy.png\n|Description  = {{C|Shiv|Shivs}} deal X additional damage.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Shiv}}\n{{C|Accuracy}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 4 (6 if upgraded) {{BD|Accuracy}}, which increases the damage of each {{C|Shiv}} by that amount.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Depends on {{C|Shiv}} cards, meaning it synergizes with sources of it:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Blade Dance}}\n* {{C|Cloak and Dagger}}\n* {{C|Infinite Blades}}\n* {{C|Storm of Steel}}\n\n==== a) Relics and Potions ====\n* {{R|Ninja Scroll}}.\n* {{P|Cunning Potion}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Accuracy card buffed. Damage increased from 3 -> 4.\n** Accuracy+ card buffed. Damage increased from 5 -> 6.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Accuracy power now correctly works with Shivs played from the top of the deck via cards like Mayhem or Havoc.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 9: Ascension'''\n** Accuracy wasn't working with Shiv+\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2034":{"pageid":2034,"ns":0,"title":"Alchemize","revisions":[{"revid":56310,"parentid":50529,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Alchemize\n| Image       = Green-Alchemize.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = Obtain a random potion.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}} \n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Alchemize}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes well with relics that improve potions, such as {{R|Toy Ornithopter}} and {{R|Sacred Bark}}.\n* {{C|Burst}} and {{P|Duplication Potion}} can be used to generate 2 random [[Potions]] instead of 1.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{P|Fruit Juice}} cannot be generated by this card, but {{P|Regen Potion}}, {{P|Blood Potion}} and {{P|Fairy in a Bottle}} can be generated.\n** However, {{P|Entropic Brew}} can be generated by this card, which can generate {{P|Fruit Juice}} while not in combat.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{R|Sozu}} fully negates this card's effect.\n\n=== Exploits ===\n* Because cards are briefly playable during {{P|Smoke Bomb}}'s escape animation, {{C|Alchemize}} can be played to regenerate the lost potion before the combat ends.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The card art as well as {{C|Alchemize}}'s internal name were both taken from a deprecated card [[Venomology]].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 54: Loop'''\n** The Specialized Daily Mod now allows Alchemize (was restricted because the mod Brewmaster used to exist).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** All sources of random temporary card generation in combat (like Dead Branch) can no longer generate cards that provide healing.\n** New tip added to indicate that healing cards cannot be generated randomly during combat.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 25: Building Blocks'''\n** Fruit Juice will no longer spawn from Alchemize.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** New green card, Alchemize. Description withheld for spoiler reasons.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2307":{"pageid":2307,"ns":0,"title":"Alpha","revisions":[{"revid":56314,"parentid":56313,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Alpha\n| Image       = Purple-Alpha.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = (;{{KW|Innate}}. <br>)Shuffle a {{C|Beta}} into your draw pile.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust, Innate\n}}\n{{C|Alpha}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It adds a {{C|Beta}} into your draw pile, which in turn adds a {{C|Omega}} to your draw pile, which in turn gives you 50 (60 if {{C|Omega}} was upgraded)) {{BD|Omega}}. {{BD|Omega}} deals damage equal to its amount to '''ALL''' enemies at the end of your turn, every turn. When upgraded, {{C|Alpha}} becomes {{KW|Innate}}, meaning it will always appear in your first hand of combat.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Beta}} and {{C|Omega}} can only be obtained in combat, they cannot be upgraded except within the combat itself. A previously played {{C|Master Reality}} will upgrade them upon being created, while {{C|Apotheosis}} or {{C|Armaments}} can upgrade them if they are respectively in your deck or hand.\n\n* Anything that allows you to dig through your draw pile synergizes well with this set of cards.\n** {{KW|Scry}} lets you get to the next card in the set quicker.\n** {{C|Omniscience}} allows you to immediately play any of the cards in the set, no matter where in your draw pile they are.\n** Cards that allow you to place cards in your hand, such as {{C|Secret Technique}} and {{C|Seek}} are also extremely helpful.\n\n{{Clear}}\n== Beta ==\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Beta\n| Image       = Colorless-Beta.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Special\n| Cost        = 2\n| CostPlus    = 1\n| Description = Shuffle an {{C|Omega}} into draw pile. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n}} \n{{C|Beta}} is a 2 (1 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It adds an {{C|Omega}} to your draw pile, which in turn gives you 50 (60 if {{C|Omega}} was upgraded)) {{BD|Omega}}. {{BD|Omega}} deals damage equal to its amount to '''ALL''' enemies at the end of your turn, every turn.\n\n{{Clear}}\n== Omega ==\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Omega\n| Image       = Colorless-Omega.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Special\n| Cost        = 3\n| Description = At the end of your turn, deal (50;60) damage to ALL enemies.\n| GivesToPlayer = Omega\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Omega\n| Image        = Icon Omega.png\n| Description  = At the end of your turn, deal X damage to ALL enemies.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n}}\n{{C|Omega}} is a 3 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colourless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 50 (60 when upgraded) {{BD|Omega}}, which deals that much damage to all enemies at the end of each turn.\n\n=== Interactions ===\n==== Order ====\n{{BD|Omega}} activates before the enemy turn. On top of happening before enemy intents, it will also activate before:\n* Before {{BD|Invincible}} resets\n* Before {{BD|Poison}} activates\n\nWhen alongside other [[Buffs]] or [[Debuffs]] which activate at the end of the player's turn, {{BD|Omega}} activates in the order the buffs were gained. This includes:\n* {{BD|The Bomb}}\n* {{BD|Regen}}\n* {{BD|Constricted}}\n* {{BD|Combust}}\n\nOther notable interactions:\n* {{BD|Blasphemer}} kills the player at the start their turn, so the player will activate {{BD|Omega}} one more time before receiving damage\n\n==== Synergies ====\n* As {{C|Omega}} can only be obtained in combat, it cannot be upgraded except within the combat itself. A previously played {{C|Master Reality}} will upgrade it upon being created, while {{C|Apotheosis}} or {{C|Armaments}} can upgrade it if it is respectively in your deck or hand.\n\n==== Neutral ====\n* This damage is not affected by {{BD|Vulnerable}}, {{BD|Strength}}, or {{BD|Double Damage}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{C|Omega}} is one of only 3 {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} in the game, the other two being {{C|Become Almighty}} and {{C|Live Forever}}. All of these cards are obtained from playing {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skills}}. However, {{C|Omega}} is the only one that can be held in hand.\n\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2035":{"pageid":2035,"ns":0,"title":"Bullet Time","revisions":[{"revid":56919,"parentid":56917,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Bullet Time\n|Image       = Green-BulletTime.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 3\n|CostPlus    = 2\n|Description = You cannot draw additional cards this turn. Reduce the cost of all cards in your hand to 0 this turn.\n|GivesToPlayer = No Draw\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|No Draw}}\n{{C|Bullet Time}} is a 3 (2 if upgraded) {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Bullet Time}} synergizes extremely well with {{R|Snecko Eye}} or a {{P|Snecko Oil}} used before it, as it benefits from the draw and completely ignores randomized energy costs by setting every card to 0 {{Icon|GE}} Energy.\n* All {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} cards set to 0 {{Icon|GE}} Energy by this card will get a damage increase from {{R|Wrist Blade}}.\n* {{R|Orange Pellets}} can remove the {{BD|No Draw}} you get from this card.\n* Sources of {{BD|Artifact}}, such as {{R|Clockwork Souvenir}}, {{P|Ancient Potion}}, {{C|Core Surge}} and {{C|Panacea}} can prevent this card from applying {{BD|No Draw}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|No Draw}} only prevents cards from being drawn, not from being generated, such as through {{R|Dead Branch}}, {{C|Distraction}} or {{C|Blade Dance}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fixed Escape Plan gaining Block when card drawn is blocked by No Draw power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 33: Terror'''\n** No Draw power now counts as a debuff.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Bullet Time now affects all cards currently in hand, works with Madness, and no longer applies a Power to you.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2424":{"pageid":2424,"ns":0,"title":"Carve Reality","revisions":[{"revid":56928,"parentid":54855,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Carve Reality\n|Image       = Purple-CarveReality.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (6;10) damage.<br>Add a {{C|Smite}} into your hand.\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Smite}}\n{{C|Carve Reality}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 (10 if upgraded) damage, and adds a {{C|Smite}} into your hand\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have played {{C|Master Reality}} before playing this card, it will add an upgraded {{C|Smite}} to your hand instead.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1934":{"pageid":1934,"ns":0,"title":"Flame Barrier","revisions":[{"revid":56758,"parentid":55781,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Flame Barrier\n|Image       = Red-FlameBarrier.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Gain (12;16) {{KW|Block}}.<br>Whenever you are attacked this turn, deal (4;6) damage back.\n|GivesToPlayer = Flame Barrier, Block\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Flame Barrier}} {{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Flame Barrier}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 12 (16 if upgraded) {{KW|Block}} and 4 (6 if upgraded) {{BD|Flame Barrier}}, which deals that amount of damage to every enemy that hits you for the rest of the turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Neutral ===\n* Only activates upon being hit by an enemy attack, so not when taking damage from:\n** {{BD|Sharp Hide}} or {{BD|Thorns}}.\n** {{BD|Explosive}}\n** {{BD|Constricted}}\n** {{BD|Beat of Death}}\n** Any damage from one of your cards, such as {{C|Burn}}, {{C|Pain}} or {{C|Bloodletting}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** WORDING: Improving consistency for Flame Barrier and Thorns wording.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Updating SFX for Flame Barrier Power.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Flame Barrier card gets a new SFX.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 36: Power Through'''\n** Thorns and Flame Barrier powers are made consistent.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Card FlameBarrier+ gets buffed. Deals 2 more damage back.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** FlameBarrier, Flight, Malleable, and Torii now have more checks to ensure that their effects trigger correctly.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2275":{"pageid":2275,"ns":0,"title":"Inner Peace","revisions":[{"revid":56624,"parentid":55826,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Inner Peace\n| Image       = Purple-InnerPeace.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = If you are in {{KW|Calm}}, draw (3;4) cards,<br>otherwise enter {{KW|Calm}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Calm, Draw\n| InteractsWith = Draw\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Calm}}\n{{C|Inner Peace}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. If you are in the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}}, it draws 3 (4 if upgraded) cards. If you were not in {{KW|Calm}} when playing this card, it makes you enter {{KW|Calm}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* When entering {{KW|Calm}} if you are not in {{KW|Calm}} yet, you will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Calm}} has certain effects:\n** Playing a successive {{C|Inner Peace}} will draw cards, meaning this card synergizes with itself, and will have a different effect if played twice, either normally or through effects such as {{C|Omniscience}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}.\n** {{BD|Like Water}} from {{C|Like Water}} will give {{KW|Block}} at the end of your turn.\n\n* Exiting {{KW|Calm}} also has the effect of giving you 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. This increases to 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows the [[Watcher]] taking a selfie in front of the Spire, holding up the peace symbol with her hand.\n** Tim Cook must have spent a lot of money to be able to sell iPhones on Preon.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2309":{"pageid":2309,"ns":0,"title":"Mental Fortress","revisions":[{"revid":55857,"parentid":55463,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Mental Fortress\n|Image       = Purple-MentalFortress.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Whenever you switch {{KW|Stance|Stances}}, gain (4;6) {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Mental Fortress}}{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Mental Fortress}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 4 (6 if upgraded) {{BD|Mental Fortress}}, which gives that amount of {{KW|Block}} every time you switch {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* When changing your {{KW|Stance}} as a result of a card, {{BD|Mental Fortress}} will activate before the card is fully resolved, meaning it can already {{KW|Block}} damage such as from {{BD|Beat of Death}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Anything that can cause you to switch {{KW|Stance}} will synergize with this card:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Empty Body}}, {{C|Empty Fist}} and {{C|Empty Mind}}, as long as you were in a {{KW|Stance}} previously.\n\n* As long as you were not in {{KW|Wrath}} previously, {{C|Eruption}}, {{C|Crescendo}}, {{C|Indignation}}, {{C|Simmering Fury}} and {{C|Tantrum}}.\n\n*  As long as you were not in {{KW|Calm}} previously, {{C|Vigilance}}, {{C|Tranquility}}, {{C|Fear No Evil}}, {{C|Inner Peace}} and {{C|Meditate}}.\n** {{C|Fear No Evil}} will only work if it is played on a target that [[Intent|Intends]] to attack.\n\n* As long as you were not in {{KW|Divinity}} previously, {{C|Prostrate}}, {{C|Pray}}, {{C|Worship}} and {{C|Devotion}} can give you enough {{BD|Mantra}} to enter {{KW|Divinity}}, and {{C|Blasphemy}} can do it directly.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Damaru}} can give you enough {{BD|Mantra}} to enter {{KW|Divinity}}.\n* {{P|Stance Potion}} will always give you the possibility to switch {{KW|Stance}}, no matter what your current {{KW|Stance}} is.\n* As long as you were not in {{KW|Divinity}} previously, {{P|Ambrosia}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gained by {{BD|Mental Fortress}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2256":{"pageid":2256,"ns":0,"title":"Overclock","revisions":[{"revid":50598,"parentid":36251,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Overclock\n|Image       = Blue-Overclock.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Draw (2;3) cards.<br>Add a {{C|Burn}} into your discard pile.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Burn}}{{C|Overclock}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 2 (3 if upgraded) cards and then adds a {{C|Burn}} to your discard pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{C|Overclock}} first draws cards and then adds a {{C|Burn}} into your discard pile, meaning there is no risk of drawing the newly added {{C|Burn}}.\n* The {{C|Burn}} gets added into your discard pile before triggering {{R|Ink Bottle}}, meaning it can be drawn if your draw pile is empty.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Hexaghost can upgrade all {{C|Burn|Burns}} in the draw and discard pile, meaning it will also upgrade {{C|Burn|Burns}} generated by this card.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* In the game code, Overclock is called Steam Power.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1863":{"pageid":1863,"ns":0,"title":"Perfected Strike","revisions":[{"revid":55475,"parentid":50400,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Perfected Strike\n|Image       = Red-PerfectedStrike.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal 6 damage.<br>Deals (2;3) additional damage for ALL your cards containing \"Strike\".\n}}\n{{C|Perfected Strike}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 6 damage, which is increased by 2 (3 if upgraded) for every card with \"Strike\" in its name that is in your deck when this card is played.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Strike Dummy}} increases the damage of this card by 3.\n\n* Any card with \"Strike\" in the name increases the damage of this card by 2 (3 if this {{C|Perfected Strike}} upgraded):\n==== Cards ====\n* All basic Strikes: {{C|Strike (Ironclad)|Strike}}, {{C|Strike (Silent)|Strike}}, {{C|Strike (Defect)|Strike}}, and {{C|Strike (Watcher)|Strike}}.\n* {{C|Perfected Strike}} increases not only the damage of other copies, but also of itself.\n* {{C|Pommel Strike}}, {{C|Twin Strike}}, {{C|Wild Strike}}.\n* {{C|Swift Strike}}.\n* {{C|Sneaky Strike}}, {{C|Thunder Strike}}, {{C|Meteor Strike}}, {{C|Windmill Strike}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The damage is calculated at the time of playing {{C|Perfected Strike}}. This means that getting rid of cards with \"Strike\" in their name during combat, such as by {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausting}}, will decrease the damage dealt by {{C|Perfected Strike}}. Similarly, increasing the amount of those cards through for example {{R|Dead Branch}} or {{C|Dual Wield}} will increase the damage.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This card's [[Beta Art]] shows a {{M|Gremlin Wizard}} admiring the [[Ironclad]]'s new sword.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** Fixed issue where Strike (blue), Thunder Strike, and Meteor Strike weren't used by Perfected Strike.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Perfected Strike now counts Strikes from other characters.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Clarified Perfected Strike's wording for new functionality.\n** Perfected Strike gets an updated description.\n** Perfected Strike reworked. Now counts ALL cards with the word Strike in its title. Swift Strike, Wild Strike, etc.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1964":{"pageid":1964,"ns":0,"title":"Poisoned Stab","revisions":[{"revid":56783,"parentid":56099,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Poisoned Stab\n|Image       = Green-PoisonedStab.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (6;8) damage.<br>Apply (3;4) {{BD|Poison}}.\n|GivesToEnemy = Poison\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Poison}}{{C|Poisoned Stab}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\nAs {{BD|Poison}} applies at the start of the enemy's turn, it has some unusual interactions:\n* If the damage is enough to cause {{M|The Guardian}} to change to Defensive form, it will immediately change its [[Intent]] to apply {{BD|Sharp Hide}}. Moreover, as it is already past the point in its turn where {{KW|Block}} is removed, it will keep the Block generated by moving to Defensive Form until its next turn.\n** Notably, in other cases where HP thresholds affect enemy [[Intent]] (such as {{M|The Champ}} and {{M|Time Eater}}), this happens on a subsequent turn, and will not be affected.\n* If the enemy dies to {{BD|Poison}}, the card drawn by {{R|Gremlin Horn}} will be held until your next turn.\n** Similarly, if a {{M|Bronze Orb}} dies while holding a card in Stasis, that card will be returned to you and stay in your hand until next turn.\n* If a {{M|Fungi Beast}} dies this way, you will receive {{BD|Vulnerable}} during the enemy turn, which may increase the amount of incoming damage for the turn.\n* If an enemy with {{BD|Minion|Minions}} dies this way, its Minions will still flee combat before attacking.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Bane}} does additional damage if the target has {{BD|Poison}}.\n* {{C|Catalyst}} can double (triple) the amount of {{BD|Poison}} on a target.\n* {{R|The Specimen}} can be used in combats with multiple enemies to consolidate {{BD|Poison}} as enemies die.\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}} applies 1 {{BD|Poison}} whenever this card applies {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n* {{C|Poisoned Stab}} works well with other sources of {{BD|Poison}}:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Deadly Poison}}, {{C|Bouncing Flask}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Corpse Explosion}}.\n* {{C|Envenom}}, which can also be triggered by this card.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Twisted Funnel}}.\n* {{P|Poison Potion}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{BD|Poison}} bypasses {{KW|Block}} and {{BD|Flying}}.\n* {{BD|Poison}} damage causes {{M|Lagavulin}} to wake up, consuming its Stunned turn in the process.\n* However, {{BD|Intangible}} reduces ''all'' sources of HP loss to 1, including {{BD|Poison}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* {{BD|Artifact}} will prevent applying {{BD|Poison}}.\n** However, as Bouncing Flask applies Poison multiple times in a single card play, it can be very effective at clearing {{BD|Artifact}} for your other {{BD|Poison}} cards.\n* Certain bosses will remove all [[Debuffs]] during combat: {{M|The Champ}}, {{M|Awakened One}}, and {{M|Time Eater}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Poisoned Stab card buff: Damage 5 -> 6. Upgraded: 6 -> 8.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1840":{"pageid":1840,"ns":0,"title":"Pommel Strike","revisions":[{"revid":56391,"parentid":50401,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Pommel Strike\n| Image       = Red-PommelStrike.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (9;10) damage.<br>Draw (1;2) (card;cards).\n| GivesToPlayer = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Pommel Strike}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 9 (10 if upgraded) damage, and draws 1 card (2 cards if upgraded).\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Pommel Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n\n* Two copies of upgraded Pommel Strike can be used to trigger {{R|Sundial}} perpetually. This combination can be further improved with something like {{R|The Abacus}} or {{R|Ornamental Fan}}.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1889":{"pageid":1889,"ns":0,"title":"Pride","revisions":[{"revid":56426,"parentid":55907,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Pride\n| Image       = Curse-Pride.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Curse\n| Cost        = 1\n| NoUpgrade   = true\n| Description = {{KW|Innate}}.<br>At the end of your turn, put a copy of this card on top of your draw pile. {{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Innate, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Pride}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. Unlike all other Curses, it can naturally be played; doing so {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} it. Pride is {{KW|Innate}}, and if it is in your hand at the end of your turn, it will put a copy of itself on top of your draw pile.\n\n== Obtaining Pride ==\nPride is exclusive to {{KW|Endless|Endless Mode}}. Every time you complete a loop of Endless Mode, [[Neow]] gives out a succession of [[Blights]] to make your run more difficult. Starting after the fourth full loop, and again on every loop after, a {{R|Grotesque Trophy}} is given to the player. On pickup, three copies of Pride are added to your deck.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Nilry's Codex}} happens ''before'' Pride. Any copies of Pride generated at end of turn will necessarily be on top of the deck.\n* Pride happens ''before'' [[Orbs#Passive|Orb Passives]]. So, if a {{KW|Lightning}} Orb kills an enemy while you have {{R|Gremlin Horn}}, you will draw the newly generated Pride before discarding for the turn.\n** As {{BD|Poison}} applies at the start of the enemy turn (rather than the end of your turn), if the enemy dies to Poison you will draw the generated Pride, and keep it until your next turn.\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Pride is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Normally, {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} would gain you max HP on picking up Pride. However, under normal circumstances you cannot obtain Pride until after four loops of Endless mode; on the third loop, you will receive {{R|Muzzle}}, which prevents increasing your max HP any more. So, in practice Darkstone Periapt no longer does anything by the time you get to Pride.\n* Despite the stated in game phrasing, only non-Curse cards are counted towards {{R|Time Maze|Time Maze's}} 15 card limit. Playing copied of Pride therefore does not count towards this limit.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Pride, it cannot be played.\n* Unlike with other Curses, which normally can't be played, {{R|Blue Candle}} actually gives a downside with Pride. Playing Pride will still cost {{Icon|CE}}, but it will ''also'' cost 1 HP.\n\n== Bugs ==\n=== Pandora's Box Skip ===\n''Main article: [[Pandora's Box#Pandora's Box Skip]]''\n\nPicking up Pride may be skipped using an exploit with the game's menu.\n* On Desktop:\n** Receive your Grotesque Trophy, so you are on the screen where you can confirm adding the copies of Pride to your deck.\n** Open up the game menu, then hit \"Abandon Run\", but '''do not confirm'''.\n** Hit the Escape key twice, bypassing the card pickup.\n* On Mobile or Desktop:\n** Receive your Grotesque Trophy, so you are on the screen where you can confirm adding the copies of Pride to your deck.\n** Open up the game menu, then hit \"Abandon Run\", but '''do not confirm'''.\n** Click on the menu gear icon again, then hit the \"Return\" button. This bypasses the card pickup, allowing you to continue past Neow.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Pride is the only Curse which can be {{KW|Transform|Transformed}}, but not Transformed into.\n* Pride's [[Beta Art]] references the fact that pride also refers to a group of lions.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1844":{"pageid":1844,"ns":0,"title":"Ritual Dagger","revisions":[{"revid":56394,"parentid":56092,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Ritual Dagger\n| Image       = Colorless-RitualDagger.png\n| Color       = Colorless\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Special\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal 15 damage. <br>If {{KW|Fatal}}, permanently increase this card's damage by (3;5).<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Fatal, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Fatal}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Ritual Dagger}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Special|Special}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 15 damage, and if this damage is {{KW|Fatal}}, it will permanently increase this damage by 3 (5 if upgraded). {{C|Ritual Dagger}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Obtaining Ritual Dagger ==\n* {{C|Ritual Dagger}} is an Event Card, and the only way to obtain one is through the event {{E|The Nest}}.\n\n* {{R|Dolly's Mirror}} can duplicate your Ritual Dagger, giving you a second copy. Do note that activating a Ritual Dagger will ''not'' affect any other copies you may have in your deck. However, the damage on the card ''will'' be copied over at the time of initial duplication, so if done late in the run, it will give a second huge Attack.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As playing {{C|Ritual Dagger}} at the right moment is crucial, it synergizes with {{R|Runic Pyramid}} and ways to {{KW|Retain}} it, such as {{C|Well-Laid Plans}}, {{C|Equilibrium}} or {{C|Meditate}}.\n\n* As one of the few cards that has benefits that remain outside of combat, triggering it as often as possible becomes an additional objective within combat. Given that {{C|Ritual Dagger}} {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} after use, it synergizes with:\n** {{R|Strange Spoon}}, which gives a 50% chance to not {{KW|Exhaust}} {{C|Ritual Dagger}} when played, allowing it to be redrawn and used again.\n** {{C|Exhume}}, which can get {{C|Ritual Dagger}} back once after being played, with the added benefit of putting it directly into your hand.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If a {{C|Ritual Dagger}} is stored using the {{E|A Note For Yourself}} event, it will not keep the damage increases, and will always do 15 damage when retrieved. As with all cards, it will retain its {{KW|Upgrade}} status.\n\n* When duplicated through an effect such as {{C|Double Tap}} or a {{P|Duplication Potion}}, {{C|Ritual Dagger}} will trigger its {{KW|Fatal}} effect even if only the second play was {{KW|Fatal}}.\n** As duplicated {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} always target the same enemy with both plays, you cannot trigger {{C|Ritual Dagger}} twice by duplicating it.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} does ''not'' trigger when {{BD|Minion|Minions}} are killed.\n** However, the {{M|Cultist}} enemies in {{M|Awakened One}} fight are not technically {{BD|Minion|Minions}}, and ''can'' trigger {{KW|Fatal}}.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} is not affected by {{M|Slime Boss}} or other Slime enemies splitting, and only triggers when reducing a Slime's health to 0, whether that Slime was spawned as the result of a split or not.\n* The first phase of {{M|Awakened One}} does not trigger {{KW|Fatal}}, but the second phase does.\n\n* In the {{M|Darkling|Three Darklings}} fight, an attack is only considered {{KW|Fatal}} if it kills the last {{M|Darkling}}; otherwise, unlimited triggers could be farmed on this fight.\n\n* {{KW|Fatal}} triggers on killing the {{M|Corrupt Heart}}, although this does not matter, as it ends the run.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Due to the limited number of {{KW|Fatal}} triggers available in any given combat, {{C|Ritual Dagger}} does not synergize with other {{KW|Fatal}} cards:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Hand of Greed}}\n* {{C|Feed}}\n* {{C|Lesson Learned}}\n\n== Trivia ==\n* A {{C|Ritual Dagger}} can be seen stuck in the {{M|Awakened One}}'s chest.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** Fatal keyword added for cards which have effects upon killing a non-Minion enemy.\n\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Automaton's orbs preventing scaling of Genetic Algorithm and Ritual Dagger.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Fixed Ritual Dagger card portrait shape.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Ritual Dagger card buff: 12 -> 15.\n** Ritual Dagger+ card buff: Upgrade amount 1 -> 2.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 34: Malaise'''\n** Ritual Dagger card buff. Base damage +3. (9 -> 12)\n** Improved formatting for Tactician and Ritual Dagger cards.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 29: TURBO'''\n** Ritual Dagger card is marked as seen when you obtain it now.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** New Card: Ritual Dagger\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1851":{"pageid":1851,"ns":0,"title":"Searing Blow","revisions":[{"revid":56399,"parentid":56044,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Searing Blow\n| Image       = Red-SearingBlow.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Deal (12;16) damage.<br>Can be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} any number of times.\n| InteractsWith = Upgrade\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Upgrade}}\n{{C|Searing Blow}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 12 damage, and can be {{KW|Upgrade|Upgraded}} any number of times to increase this damage. \n\nThe upgrade table looks as follows:\n{| class=wikitable\n!Upgrade!!Damage!!Increase\n|-\n|0 (base)||12||-\n|-\n|1||16||+4\n|-\n|2||21||+5\n|-\n|3||27||+6\n|-\n|4||34||+7\n|-\n|5||42||+8\n|-\n|6||51||+9\n|-\n|7||61||+10\n|-\n|8||72||+11\n|-\n|9||84||+12\n|-\n|10||97||+13\n|-\n|n||<math>\\frac{n(n+7)}{2} + 12</math>||n+3\n|}\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Upgrading this card in combat will increase its damage for the remainder of combat. This can be done through:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Armaments}} can upgrade it multiple times over the course of a battle.\n* {{C|Apotheosis}}\n* {{C|Master Reality}}, if {{C|Searing Blow}} is generated in combat. \n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Warped Tongs}} can upgrade it multiple times over the course of a battle.\n* {{P|Blessing of the Forge}}\n\n== Bugs ==\n* If {{C|Searing Blow}} is generated with {{BD|Master Reality}} active, it will generate with +2 {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}} instead of +1, unless generated by {{C|Foreign Influence}} or {{R|Nilry's Codex}}. \n** This can be replicated without {{R|Prismatic Shard}} or {{E|A Note For Yourself}}, by generating {{C|Searing Blow}} with {{C|Foreign Influence}} as [[The Watcher]] in the [[Bronze Automaton]] combat. Allowing one of its {{BD|Minion|Minions}} to steal {{C|Searing Blow}} and then retrieving it by killing that {{BD|Minion}} counts as that {{C|Searing Blow}} being generated.\n*** This can be used to achieve a maximum of +5 {{KW|Upgrade|Upgrades}}: +1 through initial generation via {{C|Foreign Influence}}, and +2 through both {{BD|Minion|Minions}}.\n\n== Upgrade Gallery ==\nHere are additional upgrade images:\n<gallery>\nRed-SearingBlowPlus1.png\nRed-SearingBlowPlus2.png\nRed-SearingBlowPlus3.png\nRed-SearingBlowPlus4.png\nRed-SearingBlowPlus5.png\nRed-SearingBlowPlus6.png\nRed-SearingBlowPlus7.png\nRed-SearingBlowPlus8.png\nRed-SearingBlowPlus9.png\n</gallery>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Updating VFX for Searing Blow card (now scales with upgrade count).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Adding VFX for Searing Blow card.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1921":{"pageid":1921,"ns":0,"title":"Shame","revisions":[{"revid":56750,"parentid":55937,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Shame\n|Image       = Curse-Shame.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Curse\n|Cost        = -2\n|NoUpgrade   = true\n|Description = {{KW|Unplayable}}.<br>At the end of your turn, gain 1 {{BD|Frail}}.\n|GivesToPlayer = Frail, Unplayable\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Frail}}\n{{C|Shame}} is an {{KW|Unplayable}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} Card. If it is in your hand at end of turn, it will [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] itself, and apply 1 {{BD|Frail}} to you.\n\n== Obtaining Shame ==\nLike most {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}}, Shame can be obtained from anything that gives a random Curse:\n* Can be part of Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a reward.\n* {{E|Match and Keep}}.\n* {{R|Cursed Key}}.\n* {{KW|Transform|Transforming}} another Curse.\n\nIn addition, Shame can be obtained from the {{E|Pleading Vagrant}} Event when choosing {{Frame|Rob}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* Shame will discard itself at the end of your turn before the rest of your hand, at the same time it applies the {{BD|Frail}}. This happens ''before'' {{KW|Retain}} happens, so you cannot choose to Retain it.\n<!--- I'm just including the main extra interactions here, but with the ones not relevant to the current page commented away. This allows easy transfew to related pages.--->\n* Shame, {{C|Doubt}}, {{C|Regret}}, {{C|Decay}}, and {{C|Burn|Burns}} all activate at the same time at end of turn. Visually they activate from left to right. However:\n** Regardless of the order of activation, {{C|Regret}} counts any copies of the others as being still in your hand when its damage is applied.\n<!---*** {{C|Regret}} does ''not'' take into account cards drawn from {{R|Runic Cube}} as a result of taking damage from these cards; it will always just use the number of cards in your hand when your turn ended.--->\n<!---** The damage for {{C|Decay}}, {{C|Burn}}, and {{C|Regret}} are applied from left to right. So, if you have 1 stack of {{BD|Buffer}} and two of them in hand, the left one will have its damage consumed, and the right one will apply.\n*** When selecting cards from your hand, such as to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] or {{KW|Exhaust}}, you can freely reorder your hand, as selecting and then unselecting a card moves it to the last spot in your hand. If needed, this can be used to manipulate which card's damage is applied to you.--->\n** For Shame and {{C|Doubt}}, the [[Debuffs]] are applied from left to right. So, if you have 1 stack of {{BD|Artifact}} and both in hand, the left one will consume the Artifact and the right one will apply.\n*** When selecting cards from your hand, such as to [[Keywords#Discard|discard]] or {{KW|Exhaust}}, you can freely reorder your hand, as selecting and then unselecting a card moves it to the last spot in your hand. If needed, this can be used to manipulate which Curse's debuff is applied to you.\n\n=== Synergies ===\nAs Shame is a '''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}''', it interacts with the following:\n* {{C|Fire Breathing}} will deal damage when it is drawn.\n* {{R|Du-Vu Doll}} will give you 1 {{BD|Strength}} each combat.\n* {{R|Blue Candle}} can be used to {{KW|Exhaust}} it for 1 HP. \n* When added to the deck, it will be negated by {{R|Omamori}}, or gain you 6 max HP if you have {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} and ''not'' Omamori.\n\nThe {{BD|Frail}} debuff can be dealt with in a few ways:\n* It can be prevented with sources of {{BD|Artifact}}, such as {{C|Core Surge}} and {{C|Panacea}}.\n* It can be removed during your next turn with {{R|Orange Pellets}}.\n* The downside can be ignored by having a {{KW|Block}} plan that doesn't require Block cards, such as {{C|After Image}}, {{C|Apparition}}, {{C|Wraith Form}}, {{KW|Frost|Frost Orbs}}, or {{C|Buffer}}.\n* {{C|Barricade}} can carry {{KW|Block}} between turns, reducing the impact of a single turn of {{BD|Frail}}.\n* {{C|Vault}} can be used to skip to your next turn, clearing the debuff without giving the enemy a chance to attack first.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Shame cannot be {{KW|Retain|Retained}}, and does not stay in your hand with {{R|Runic Pyramid}}, as it discards itself as part of its end of turn activation.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Clash}} can only be played when all cards in your hand are {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}}, if it is drawn at the same time as Shame, it cannot be played.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1864":{"pageid":1864,"ns":0,"title":"Shockwave","revisions":[{"revid":56407,"parentid":55938,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Shockwave\n| Image       = Red-Shockwave.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 2\n| Description = Apply (3;5) {{BD|Weak}} and {{BD|Vulnerable}} to ALL enemies.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n| GivesToEnemy = Weak, Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Weak}} {{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Shockwave}} is a 2 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It applies 3 (5 if upgraded) {{BD|Weak}} and 3 (5 if upgraded) {{BD|Vulnerable}} to '''ALL''' enemies. {{C|Shockwave}} will then {{KW|Exhaust}} itself.\n\n== Interactions == \n=== Order ===\n* The {{BD|Weak}} applies first and the {{BD|Vulnerable}} applies afterwards, meaning enemies with one {{BD|Artifact}} will only receive the {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Phrog}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Dropkick, Fire Breathing, and Shockwave portraits weren't rendering in card popup view.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2432":{"pageid":2432,"ns":0,"title":"Slimed","revisions":[{"revid":50789,"parentid":50715,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Slimed\n|Image       = Colorless-Slimed.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Status\n|Rarity      = Status\n|Cost        = 1\n|NoUpgrade   = true\n|Description = {{KW|Exhaust}}.\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Slimed}} is a 1 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} Card. Slimed is the ONLY playable {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Status|Status}} card.\n\n== Obtaining Slimed ==\nThe following enemies can give the player {{C|Slimed}}:\n* {{M|Spike Slime (L)}}\n** {{Int|Spike Slime (L)|Flame Tackle}} - Adds 2 {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Spike Slime (M)}}\n** {{Int|Spike Slime (M)|Flame Tackle}} - Adds a {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Acid Slime (L)}}\n** {{Int|Acid Slime (L)|Corrosive Spit}} - Adds 2 {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Acid Slime (M)}}\n** {{Int|Acid Slime (M)|Corrosive Spit}} - Adds a {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Slime Boss}}\n** {{Int|Slime Boss|Goop Spray}} - Adds 3({{Asc|19|5}}) {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Time Eater}} '''Only above {{Asc|19|Ascension}}.'''\n** {{Int|Time Eater|Head Slam}} - Adds 2 {{C|Slimed}} into your discard pile.\n* {{M|Corrupt Heart}}\n** {{Int|Corrupt Heart|Debilitate}} - Adds 1 {{C|Slimed}} into your draw pile.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Triggers the damage from {{C|Fire Breathing}}.\n* Draws cards with {{C|Evolve}}.\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} by {{C|Second Wind}} and triggers its {{KW|Block}} gain.\n* Can be {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} to trigger exhaust synergies such as {{C|Feel No Pain}} or {{R|Charon's Ashes}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Is {{KW|Exhaust|exhausted}} by {{C|Sever Soul}} since it's not an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* Prevents {{C|Clash}} from being played.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Medical Kit relic will no longer cause Slimed cards to glow as if they could be played when you have no energy.\n** Medical Kit will no longer allow the player to sometimes play Slimed when out of energy.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 17: Patched in the Face'''\n** Slimed: Replaces Wounds and Draw Reduction debuff from Slime enemies.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2078":{"pageid":2078,"ns":0,"title":"Sweeping Beam","revisions":[{"revid":50570,"parentid":36226,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Sweeping Beam\n|Image       = Blue-SweepingBeam.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (6;9) damage to ALL enemies.<br>Draw 1 card.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Sweeping Beam}} is a 1 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 53: Blizzard'''\n** Adding a VFX for Sweeping Beam card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Adding SFX for Sweeping Beam card.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1866":{"pageid":1866,"ns":0,"title":"Thunderclap","revisions":[{"revid":56406,"parentid":55979,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Thunderclap\n| Image       = Red-Thunderclap.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = Deal (4;7) damage and apply 1 {{BD|Vulnerable}} to ALL enemies.\n| GivesToEnemy = Vulnerable\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Vulnerable}}{{C|Thunderclap}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 4 (7 if upgraded) damage and applies 1 {{BD|Vulnerable}} to '''ALL''' enemies.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{R|Paper Phrog}} increases the effectiveness of {{BD|Vulnerable}}.\n* {{R|Champion Belt}} will apply 1 {{BD|Weak}} to '''ALL''' enemies to whom the {{BD|Vulnerable}} successfully applies.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Thunderclap VFX no longer appears on dead enemies during multi-enemy combats.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}